WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.380
- My daughter, my youngest
daughter, loves doing makeup.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.920
Do your daughters love doing makeup?

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.430
- My oldest daughter is a bit of an artist

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.620
and she likes doing more fantasy makeup.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.344
So right now she's into TikTok.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.842
(audience laughs)

00:00:12.842 --> 00:00:13.700
- Oh my God that's so cool!

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.196
- And she likes doing graphic design,

00:00:16.196 --> 00:00:20.150
and so this is her doing graphic
design makeup on herself,

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.950
but she also likes to do,

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.990
it looks kind of like anime-ish,

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.180
clownish, with like,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.890
she puts freckles on herself,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.700
and like orange blush.
- I love that.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.004
- It's fine. (audience laughs)

00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:34.610
- I walked in the other day,

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.480
my daughter was getting ready
like for school or whatever,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.170
and I swear she got
into some kind of makeup

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.210
I didn't know she had,

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.301
and she looked like Mimi
from the Drew Carey Show.

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:44.072
(audience laughs)

00:00:44.072 --> 00:00:46.520
- I love Mimi! (laughs)

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.180
- I was like, I was like--

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.940
- That is a strong choice.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.830
- It's a good solid reference of like,

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:52.760
it's what she looked like.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.617
And I was like,

00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:56.330
"You look so beautiful."

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:57.832
I was like, "It's great!"

00:00:57.832 --> 00:00:59.930
- I have no problem telling my child

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:02.461
that she's not allowed to leave
the house looking like that.

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.360
- I have no problem either.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.490
- When she does the whole...

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.330
- But it's kind of fun

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.741
because it brings out the artist in them,

00:01:07.741 --> 00:01:08.720
it's cool.
- Yeah, and I think

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.410
it's fine for her to play, and explore.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:13.560
- So you've described them actually,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.450
that they have bleeding
hearts, your children.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.651
- They do, they're the opposite of me.

00:01:17.651 --> 00:01:19.560
(Kelly and the audience laugh)

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.990
No, I mean I started working
when I was very young,

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.393
and my dad, I think he wanted a boy,

00:01:25.455 --> 00:01:26.700
and so while he grew,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.050
you know he raised me,
he's a feminist, my father,

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.870
he always said women deserve
equal parts in the world,

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:33.960
- I love your dad!
- in society,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.845
and everything an much as men.

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:36.810
(audience cheers)

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.280
And so he always encouraged me to step up,

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.610
but especially in sports, even
though I was a sickly kid,

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.780
he was like, "You're not gonna throw,"

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.500
you know, he would say, "Not
gonna throw like a girl."

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.860
Which at the time, you know,

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.693
now I'm like,

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:51.840
"Well, a little bit weird
for you to say that."

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.660
But you know, at the
time he was just saying

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.550
I want you to be at the top level

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.660
of whoever it is you're doing sports with.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.120
So, yeah,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.110
- I love your dad!
- I kind of have

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.810
this more kind of like rough exterior.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.223
I have a more, you know,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.110
you don't show your emotions,

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.278
you just kind of keep it all in.

00:02:11.278 --> 00:02:12.190
And it's like--
- Oh gosh,

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.755
I could never be Latino.
- It's a Catholic thing.

00:02:13.755 --> 00:02:15.210
(audience laughs)

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.680
Yeah, and some of it's more like,

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.440
you know, you don't tell
people your business,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.366
and if you have a problem,
talk to the priest!

00:02:20.366 --> 00:02:21.504
(Kelly and the audience laugh)

00:02:21.504 --> 00:02:23.350
- We are so opposite!

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.360
- Yeah I know, that was how I was sort of,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.193
you know, grew up.

00:02:26.193 --> 00:02:28.360
- I'm like TMI, I give way too much away.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.193
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.193 --> 00:02:30.720
- Maybe we should hang out.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.700
You could use a little more of this

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:32.780
and I could use a little more of that.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.260
- We could do a mix.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.420
- But you said your kids
are actually the opposite?

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.356
- So my kids came out
and everything is like,

00:02:39.356 --> 00:02:41.345
"Ugh!" (audience laughs)

00:02:41.345 --> 00:02:42.407
- They're me.
- Everything is like,

00:02:42.407 --> 00:02:43.430
"Oh Gosh!"
- It's drama.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.770
- [Jessica] And I'm like, "What happened?"

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:47.840
And it's like, "My shoelace broke."

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.987
And I'm like, "What? Your shoelace?

00:02:49.987 --> 00:02:51.050
"Get another shoelace!"

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.620
It's like, what is going on?

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.811
Anyway, so they--

00:02:53.811 --> 00:02:54.920
- They're dramatic.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.670
- They're very dramatic.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.900
But it's nice for me

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.230
because then it forces
me to open my heart,

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.760
and to have compassion

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.910
and empathy for people who
are operating in the world

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.290
very differently to me.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.191
- Yeah, like me.

00:03:07.191 --> 00:03:08.724
(audience laughs)

00:03:08.724 --> 00:03:09.557
- Exactly like you!

00:03:09.557 --> 00:03:11.147
I basically gave birth to you.

00:03:11.147 --> 00:03:12.766
- You basically did.

00:03:12.766 --> 00:03:15.350
It's full on karma happening
at my house though,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.460
my kids are identical to me,

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.319
and I'm like, "Get over it!"

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:20.260
(audience laughs)
I'm so dramatic.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.093
But I love,

00:03:21.093 --> 00:03:23.630
you posted recently, it was
a pretty great mommy moment.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.820
- Which one? (audience laughs)

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:27.935
- It might involve your son.
- Oh!

00:03:27.935 --> 00:03:30.953
And it might involve poo.
- Poo.

00:03:30.953 --> 00:03:31.786
Poo.

00:03:31.786 --> 00:03:32.800
Yeah, in the bathtub.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.940
- I mean let's talk about it.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.160
- I just, it was so gross.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.284
- Does it happen often?

00:03:36.284 --> 00:03:37.703
(audience laughs)

00:03:37.703 --> 00:03:40.223
- I think when he just
gets real comfortable.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.520
So I know if there's like,

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.320
more than 10 minutes in the bathtub,

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.760
it's happening.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.593
He just like gets--

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:48.583
- Look at her!

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:52.733
Your daughters have zero time,
- They have no time.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.210
- They have zero time for this.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.610
Oh my God I don't know what I'd do,

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.590
I think I'd laugh so
hard I would pee my pants

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.360
if my son did that. (audience laughs)

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.193
I think I might applaud it.

00:04:02.193 --> 00:04:04.537
- So, what I said to the girls was like,

00:04:04.537 --> 00:04:08.067
"Not only did you poo
on me, and barf on me

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:10.540
"several times throughout your babyhood."

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.760
'cause my kids get sick, motion sickness,

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.363
so every car ride, every train ride.

00:04:15.363 --> 00:04:16.580
- Oh my God, that's horrible.
- Every plane ride,

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.810
every single one, it's coming out.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.360
And so I was like,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.904
and whilst in the bathtub with me.

00:04:23.904 --> 00:04:25.810
- Oh no.
- That's fun, too.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:29.440
So I'm like, "You guys need
to help me clean this up."

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.125
And they were like, "Gross, Mom!"

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:33.050
And so I made them.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.980
- I love the eye roll, from the eldest.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.570
That's my favorite, that was my favorite.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.403
- She was like, "Ugh!"

00:04:37.403 --> 00:04:38.730
- When you started your company

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.675
it was a very different world than kind of

00:04:40.675 --> 00:04:43.240
what we're talking about in
our social climate right now.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.900
Like for a woman to be heading

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.480
a billion dollar industry is kind of hard.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.120
I mean, what are the challenges of that?

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.370
- Well,

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.203
gosh.

00:04:51.203 --> 00:04:53.970
I mean, even eight to ten years ago,

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.901
raising money for a new business

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:59.440
was really, really hard for a woman.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.330
And you know, even though
women start businesses

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:03.690
three times more than men,

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:08.003
even now less than two
percent get funding,

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.140
by the venture capital
to start their companies.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:17.140
And so there's just a huge
inequality in all of it.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:20.990
And certainly in corporate
America, and government,

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.710
you know, it's like a really,

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.220
even though we're half the
population we aren't really seen,

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.700
and we're not really treated equally.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:28.660
- Or feel represented.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.395
- And we don't feel
represented, because we aren't.

00:05:31.395 --> 00:05:35.280
Yet we have spending power, ladies!

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.275
Ladies, we control the pocketbook!

00:05:37.275 --> 00:05:38.245
(audience applauds)

00:05:38.245 --> 00:05:40.700
And so, once I just,

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:44.390
once I really just kind of tapped in to

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:47.000
if I was gonna dream and create something,

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.030
I mean, it was crazy that I thought

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.520
that I could even become
successful as an actress.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.280
I come from a very, you
know, modest background,

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.420
in the suburbs of L.A.,

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.930
and I was this kid with this
dream, and I figured it out.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:01.800
I guess I had this fearlessness

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:05.240
and this dream that I
could create this company

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.220
that represents

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.053
women,

00:06:08.053 --> 00:06:09.535
that stands for human health,

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.580
that has high standards

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.080
and transparency around how we operate.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.380
And can be a global brand.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.375
- And you care.

00:06:17.375 --> 00:06:18.409
But that's the thing about your products,

00:06:18.409 --> 00:06:20.317
you care.
- I do care. I really do.

